course: dictionary
lesson: 8844
title: One word, two meanings: shiva
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning the writer means. «Jewish families sit shiva, a week of mourning at home, when friends visit with food and comfort.» Mourning, at home and friends visiting are the clues. So shiva here means a time of grieving after someone dies.
explain: Now read a different sentence: «Shiva is one of the most important gods in Hinduism.» The capital letter, the word gods and the word Hinduism are the clues. This shiva is a name, not a time of mourning. Always ask: what meaning fits these clues best?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Families sit a seven-day time of mourning at home» sounds odd, but «Jewish families sit shiva, a week of mourning at home» makes sense. If the swapped sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Shiva with a capital letter is the name of a Hindu god, or of a person.
fact: «Sit shiva» means the seven days of mourning after a close relative dies, when the family stays at home and friends visit.
fact: Shiva is one of the three main gods in Hinduism, with Brahma and Vishnu.
fact: Hindus believe Shiva is both a destroyer and a renewer.
fact: The word for mourning, shiva, comes from the Hebrew word for seven.
exercise: «Jewish families sit shiva, a week of mourning at home, when friends visit with food and comfort.» What does shiva mean in this sentence? | *A seven-day time of mourning after a death, when friends visit | A Hindu prayer for the new year | A type of Jewish bread | A festival of lights
exercise: «Shiva is one of the most important gods in Hinduism.» Find and copy one word that tells you Shiva is a god. | important | *gods | one | Hinduism
exercise: In «sit shiva», the word shiva has no capital letter. What does that tell you? | It is a person's name | It means a party | It is the name of a god | *It is a common noun, a time of mourning
test: Hindus believe Shiva is both a destroyer and a renewer. What does renewer suggest? | Someone who breaks things | A cook who makes sandwiches | A bird that sings in spring | *Someone who makes things new again
test: «Afterwards there is often a wake, sandwiches and cake at a pub or a hall, where grown-ups laugh, cry and share stories.» Which clue tells you a wake is a gathering, not a race? | *Grown-ups laugh, cry and share stories | The word pub | The word sandwiches | The word wake, on its own
exam: Which clue best shows that «shiva» means a time of mourning and not a god? | The word shiva is in a sentence | The family goes to the seaside | *Friends visit with food and comfort, at home | Shiva is a Hindu god
